You are working on a branch that is adding virtual shards to Vitess.

Historically in Vitess each vttablet + mysqlctl process has only managed one shard (contained in one MySQL schema). With virtual shards, a keyspace can be designated as a "virtual keyspace" which means that it is assigned to an existing physical keyspace.

Virtual keyspaces are not health checked by vtgate, and the physical keyspace they belong to is designated in the topology service.